// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v3.1.16 — Daily Loss Limit (DLL) soft gate (Jul 10 2026)
// - Adds a configurable per-session dollar loss gate that blocks new entries
//   when cumulative realized P&L for the session drops below i_dailyLossLimit.
// - Uses strategy.netprofit minus a session-start snapshot (v3_sessionPnlStart)
//   captured at the 17:00 CT ETH open bar — giving true intraday P&L.
// - Gate is symmetric: blocks both bull and bear new entries. Does NOT close any
//   open position — broker SL/TP handles that.
// - DLL = 0.0 disables the gate entirely (default off for safety on upgrade).
// - HUD row 14 added: shows session P&L and OPEN/BLOCKED status in diagnostics table.
// - Kept in lockstep with v4.1.16 which uses v4_runningPnl for the same gate.
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v3.1.16 — MGC regime gate ON + MGC loss policy ON (Jul 9 2026)
// - mgc_useRegime: false -> true. Enabled at shared i_regimeMinScore=4.
//   Live data analysis (Jun 22 – Jul 9, 98 trades): 14 counter-regime trades
//   produced -$1,423 vs +$2,914 from 62 aligned trades. Jun 24 blowup (-$1,014)
//   was two MGC shorts fired into STRONG BULL (+6) regime — gate would have
//   blocked both. Forward-validate at Oct 1 refit (same protocol as MES gate).
// - mgc_lossPolicy: false -> true. Defense-in-depth alongside the regime gate.
//   Prior backtest rejection (v3.1.12) was against the thin 26-trade external-
//   sweep params (now superseded by v3.1.6 re-optimization). Re-evaluate at Oct 1.
// - No other changes. Re-create TV alerts on MGC charts after swap.
// ============================================================
