// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v3.0.1 — Decouple DOW presets from block-window filter
// - FIX: Day-of-week preset loading is no longer tied to "Use Optimized Time Filter".
//   In v3.0.0 that single flag controlled BOTH intraday block windows AND DOW presets,
//   so you could not load optimized DOW days without also forcing the preset block
//   windows on (and vice versa).
// - NEW INPUT: i_useOptimizedDOW ("Use Optimized DOW Defaults", Day of Week Filter group).
//     ON  -> load per-instrument DOW presets (MNQ: Sun/Mon/Thu OFF; MGC: Sun/Mon/Fri OFF).
//     OFF -> use the manual Trade [Day] toggles. Default OFF (preserves v3.0.0 behavior).
//   Requires i_useDOW ON to have any effect (i_useDOW remains the master DOW gate).
// - "Use Optimized Time Filter" (i_useOptimizedTimeFilter) now governs intraday block
//   windows ONLY, as it did pre-v3.0.0.
// - MIGRATION: if a chart had "Use Optimized Time Filter" ON specifically to load DOW
//   presets, also tick "Use Optimized DOW Defaults" to keep the same day blocking.
// - No change to dowAllowed gate logic, preset values, or signal/exit logic.
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v3.0.0 — Day of Week Filter
// - NEW: Day of Week (DOW) filter with per-instrument optimized defaults.
//   6 days: Sun/Mon/Tue/Wed/Thu/Fri. Sunday = Globex open session.
//   When i_useOptimizedTimeFilter ON: preset DOW defaults load automatically.
//   When OFF: user configures each day manually via i_trade* toggles.
//   MNQ defaults: Sun/Mon/Thu OFF (losing days per analysis). Tue/Wed/Fri ON.
//   MGC defaults: Sun/Mon/Fri OFF. Tue/Wed/Thu ON.
//   MES/M2K/SIL: all days ON (insufficient data to justify blocking).
//   Wired into entryTimeAllowed — zero impact on exit logic or EOD behavior.
//   DOW status shown in filter display (fltTxt) when enabled.
//
// RELEASE NOTES v2.1.0 — GAS alert() calls gated to Google Sheets Webhook mode only
// - Fixed: sheetsLongEntryMsg, sheetsShortEntryMsg, and exitLogMsg alert() calls
//   were firing unconditionally regardless of webhook mode setting
// - Root cause: users running Ghost Webhook mode were getting double-fired alerts —
//   Ghost received both the strategy.entry() alert_message AND the GAS alert()
//   payload, causing duplicate orders
// - Fix: all three alert() call sites now gated behind isSheetsWebhook check
//   · Ghost Webhook mode: zero alert() calls fire — Ghost only sees strategy.entry/exit
//   · Google Sheets Webhook mode: all alert() calls fire as before → GAS logging
//   · Ninja-View mode: NV payloads unchanged, GAS entry alerts also gated
// - No changes to strategy logic, entry/exit behavior, or any other functionality
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v2.0.7 — EOD info panel stale display fix
// - Fixed: info panel showed "Open — LONG/SHORT" with TP/SL/ATR rows visible
//   during the 15:50–17:00 CDT EOD window even after EOD close fired
// - Root cause: isFlat derives from strategy.position_size which stays non-zero
//   after EOD strategy.close_all() until Pine internally confirms the close
// - Fix: isFlat now includes `or eodReached` — panel displays Flat state
//   immediately at 15:50 CDT when EOD window opens, regardless of position_size
// - All table rows (Position, Contracts, Buy/Sell Price, ATR, TP, SL, Exit Mode)
//   flip to EOD/flat display automatically via single isFlat definition change
// - No changes to entry/exit logic, alerts, presets, or any other behavior
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v2.0.6 — ETH session open stale position fix
// - Fixed: Pine strategy position tracker could carry stale state from prior
//   session (e.g. Friday EOD close) into ETH open (17:00 CDT), blocking new
//   entries until a TP/SL hit forced an internal tracker reset
// - Root cause: EOD strategy.close_all() fires at 15:50 CDT and Ghost executes
//   the close, but Pine receives no fill confirmation — position_size stays
//   non-zero across the weekend gap
// - Fix: added ETH session open guard — at the first confirmed 17:00 CDT bar,
//   if position_size != 0, strategy.close_all() fires with "SESSION-Stale"
//   comment to flush Pine's internal tracker
// - Ghost is already flat (EOD fired Friday) — this is a Pine-only reset
// - ethFlatFired guard prevents re-firing; resets each day at EOD window open
// - No changes to entry/exit logic, presets, or any other behavior
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v2.0.5 — XAUUSD preset consolidation
// - Removed old XAUUSD 5m preset (Python-optimized 2020-2024, confluence path)
