//   - One-bar calculation lag but visual placement is on the correct bar/price
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v1.3.9 — Ghost Webhook SL/TP reverted to absolute prices
//
// - Reverted Ghost entry payload tp/sl back to absolute price levels
//   Testing confirmed Ghost passes distance values directly to Tradovate
//   as absolute prices — does NOT add distance to fill price internally
//   Result: stop placed at 110.00 instead of entry - 110 points (wrong)
// - Back to: "tp":<longTP1/shortTP1>, "sl":<longSL1/shortSL1>
//   These are signal-bar close ± ATR distance — small offset from actual
//   fill price (1-3 ticks on 5m bars) but far better than raw distances
// - Ghost settings remain:
//     Webhook Controls Contracts = CHECKED
//     Use Stop Loss & Take Profit = CHECKED
//     Use Webhook SL/TP          = CHECKED
//   Ghost reads absolute price levels from payload and places bracket orders
//   directly at those prices in Tradovate — intrabar execution confirmed
// - Adjusted spacing in display table
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v1.3.8 — Ghost Webhook SL/TP sends point distances
//
// - Changed Ghost entry payload tp/sl fields from absolute price levels
//   to ATR-based point distances from entry
// - Previous: "tp":6715.84,"sl":6634.62 (absolute prices — Ghost ignored or
//   misinterpreted as distances, causing immediate bracket errors)
// - Now:      "tp":25.75,"sl":55.50 (point distances — matches Ghost spec)
// - Ghost "Use Webhook SL/TP" checkbox confirmed to expect point distances
//   per Quantcrawler team (John MOD)
// - Distances are ATR-based: tp = atrVal × p_tp1, sl = atrVal × p_sl1
//   Same values Pine Script uses internally for strategy.exit() bracket
// - Ghost settings required:
//     Webhook Controls Contracts = CHECKED
//     Use Stop Loss & Take Profit = CHECKED
//     Use Webhook SL/TP          = CHECKED
// - MES preset re-optimized on clean live data (Jan 25–Mar 23 2026):
//     RSI Length 14→11, RSI OB 70→60, SL1 2.25→2.00, TP1 1.05→1.00
//     Result: PF 1.811, Win 78.0%, DD 0.46% (was PF 1.244, Win 71.5%)
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v1.3.7 — Ghost Webhook SL/TP bracket support
//
// GHOST BRACKET FIX:
// - Added "tp" and "sl" price fields to Ghost entry payloads
// - Ghost entry payload now: {"ticker":"<sym>","action":"buy","price":<p>,"qty":<n>,"tp":<tp>,"sl":<sl>}
// - Ghost short entry:       {"ticker":"<sym>","action":"sell","price":<p>,"qty":<n>,"tp":<tp>,"sl":<sl>}
// - TP and SL values are ATR-based estimates from signal-bar close
//   (actual fill price not available until next bar — signal-bar estimates
//   are typically 1-3 ticks off, far better than 5-minute bar-close lag)
// - Ghost ticker settings — THREE checkboxes required:
//     Webhook Controls Contracts = CHECKED
//     Use Stop Loss & Take Profit = CHECKED
//     Use Webhook SL/TP          = CHECKED  ← NEW requirement
//   Ghost reads sl/tp from payload and places live intrabar bracket orders
//   in Tradovate immediately at entry. Falls back to configured distances
//   if payload does not include sl/tp fields.
// - Pine Script strategy.exit() bracket still placed internally for
//   backtest accuracy and as a safety fallback
// - Reset baseline for MES
// - Added display of version # to main display panel
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v1.3.6 — Ghost webhook rebuilt + Webhook Mode selector
//
// WEBHOOK MODE SELECTOR (new):
// - Added "📡 Webhook Mode" dropdown to ⚡ Preset group with two options:
//     Ghost Webhook:         fires Ghost-compatible JSON on entry, exit, and EOD
//     Google Sheets Webhook: fires full AlertLog (entry) + TradeLog (exit) payloads
//   Modes are mutually exclusive — select one per chart
//   Ninja-View mode is unaffected by this setting
//
// GHOST WEBHOOK REBUILT (community contribution — finalpsion09):
// - Replaced standalone ghost alert() calls with alert_message= pattern on
//   strategy.entry() and strategy.exit() — fires precisely when Pine Script
//   actually enters or exits, eliminating any timing gap
// - Ghost entry payload: {"ticker":"<syminfo.ticker>","action":"buy","price":<p>,"qty":<n>}
// - Ghost short entry:   {"ticker":"<syminfo.ticker>","action":"sell","price":<p>,"qty":<n>}
// - Ghost exit payload:  {"ticker":"<syminfo.ticker>","action":"exit"}
//   Carried on all strategy.exit() calls including TP1, TP2, SL, and BE stops
// - Standalone alert() also fires on entry bar for redundancy —
//   Ghost deduplicates automatically (rejects duplicate within 60s)
// - EOD close fires exit payload to Ghost regardless of Pine position state —
//   safety net guarantees broker is flat even if EOD fires on flat position
// - Uses syminfo.ticker (e.g. "MES1!") — Ghost accepts continuous contract format
// - Ghost ticker settings: Webhook Controls Contracts = CHECKED,
//                          Use Stop Loss & Take Profit = UNCHECKED
//   Ghost relies entirely on Pine Script to signal entries and exits
//
// GOOGLE SHEETS WEBHOOK (unchanged behavior, now explicit mode):
// - Entry: full AlertLog JSON payload fires on entry bar (mode, ticker, price, tp, sl, etc.)
// - Exit:  full TradeLog JSON payload fires on position close (entry/exit/PnL data)
// - EOD:   eod_close payload fires to AlertLog
// - Ninja-View AlertLog entry payload unchanged — fires alongside NV OCO payload
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v1.3.5 — Ghost exit alerts + fill-price bracket fix
//
// GHOST EXIT ALERTS (new):
// - Ghost Mode now fires a close alert to the Ghost webhook when a
//   position closes at TP or SL — this is required for Ghost to flatten
//   the broker position when "Webhook Controls Contracts" is CHECKED and
//   "Use Stop Loss & Take Profit" is UNCHECKED (correct Ghost config)
// - Ghost close payload: {"action":"close","alert_type":"tp_sl_close","ticker":"<sym>"}
// - Alert 3 added to Ghost Mode chart setup — same Ghost webhook URL as Alert 1
// - EOD close alert was already present and unchanged
// - Ghost ticker settings: Webhook Controls Contracts = CHECKED,
//   Use Stop Loss & Take Profit = UNCHECKED (Ghost relies on Pine Script
//   to fire exit signals — no internal bracket placed by Ghost)
//
// FILL-PRICE BRACKET FIX (contributed by community member, based on v1.4.0):
// - TP1, SL1, TP2 exit orders now placed AFTER position opens, using
//   strategy.position_avg_price (actual fill price) instead of signal-bar close
// - ATR distances frozen at signal time via persistent vars
//   (entry_tp1_dist, entry_sl1_dist, entry_tp2_dist) so ATR doesn't
//   drift on later bars
// - Breakeven logic uses stored distances for TP2 target recalculation
// - Trade level lines updated to use actual fill price + stored distances
// - Exit webhook TP/SL fields now reflect actual bracket prices from fill
// - Webhook entry payload TP/SL fields remain signal-bar estimates
//   (actual bracket placed from real fill price on next bar)
// - Fixes: premature stops, missed targets, SL/TP drift from anchoring
//   exit prices to signal-bar close instead of actual entry price
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v1.3.4 — Ticker auto-calc roll logic fix
// - Fixed quarterly roll logic for MES, MNQ, M2K
//   Previously rolled on Monday after third Friday — caused near-expiry
//   execution failures as NT8 rejects low-liquidity expiring contracts
// - Now rolls to next contract on day 10 of the expiry month
//   Day 10 aligns with typical volume crossover (new contract volume
//   exceeds old contract volume ~second Thursday of expiry month)
// - Fixed bi-monthly roll logic for MGC with same day-10 threshold
// - Year rollover handled correctly: Dec → Mar rolls to next calendar year
// - NV Ticker Override field remains available for manual correction
//   near any roll date where auto-calc needs adjustment
// ============================================================
// RELEASE NOTES v1.3.3 — Account selection clarification
// - Added inline code comments above i_nv_account explaining account selection
//   architecture for all three modes:
//   Ghost Mode:     account configured in Ghost dashboard — no Pine Script input needed
//   TV Native Mode: account selected via TradingView Trade panel — no Pine Script input needed
//   Ninja-View Mode: account must be specified in NV Account field — NT8 is not visible to TV
// - Improved i_nv_account tooltip with clear instructions:
//   where to find the account string in NT8 (Control Center → Accounts)
//   when to use Sim101 vs prop firm string
//   that Ghost and TV Native do not use this field
